course: dictionary
lesson: 12700
title: Documentation: proof, instructions and records
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Documentation is a long word, but it is a useful one. It means official papers, records or written information that prove something or explain how something works. «You will need your passport and proper documentation to fly abroad.» A passport proves who you are, so here documentation means papers that prove something.
explain: «The new game came with documentation that showed how to play.» A booklet that explains how something works is documentation too. The clues are the words how to play, which tell you the papers are instructions.
explain: Documentation can also mean recording what happens. «The scientists kept careful documentation of every test, with notes and photos.» Here it means written, photo or video records of facts and events. Ask yourself: is this a paper that proves something, a set of instructions, or a record of what happened?
fact: Documentation means official papers or records that prove something, such as passports, certificates or receipts.
fact: Documentation can also mean written instructions or information that explain how something works, such as a manual for a program.
fact: Documentation can mean recording facts or events in writing, photos or video.
fact: Phrases to know: «proper documentation», «supporting documentation» and «software documentation».
fact: Documentation is uncountable, so say «some documentation», not «a documentation» or «documentations».
exercise: «You will need your passport and proper documentation to fly abroad.» What is the documentation here? | A map of the airport | *Official papers that prove who you are | A holiday in the sun | A fast plane with big wings
exercise: «The new game came with documentation that showed how to play.» What is the documentation? | A loud noise from the box | A prize for winning the game | *Written instructions that explain how something works | A piece of the game board
exercise: Which word in «The scientists kept careful documentation of every test» means written records? | scientists | kept | every | *documentation
test: «Careful documentation of the experiment was kept in a notebook, with photos.» What does documentation mean here? | A sharp tool for cutting | A loud noise in the lab | *Written and photo records of what happened | A game played by the team
test: Which is the best example of documentation? | A song on the radio | A glass of milk | A pair of football boots | *A passport with your photo in it
exam: Which sentence uses documentation correctly? | We need three documentations for the trip | We need a documentation for the trip | We need documentations for the trip | *We need some documentation for the trip
